font must not use the Reserved Font Names. Using them inside a document — which
is what this tool does — is unrestricted.

## Bundled into every built book

A book produced by this tool is one self-contained HTML file, which means these
are compiled into it. Sending someone a book sends them these too.

| Library | Licence | What it does in the book |
|---|---|---|
| [page-flip](https://github.com/Nodlik/StPageFlip) | MIT | the page-turn geometry — the bend, the shadow, the spine |
| [GSAP](https://gsap.com) | GreenSock standard "no charge" | the opening sequence and every content reveal |
| [curtains.js](https://www.curtainsjs.com) | MIT | the WebGL cloth on the opening curtain |

### GSAP is the one to actually read

Every other dependency here is MIT or ISC. GSAP is not. The package carries
`@license Copyright 2026 — Subject to the terms at https://gsap.com/standard-license`.

The standard licence permits free use in most projects, including commercial
ones, but it is **not** an open-source licence and it has conditions — notably
around products where the animation itself is the thing being sold. Recorded
here rather than buried in a minified bundle, so anyone shipping books made
with this can check it against their own use before, rather than after.

